<LegalPage
  appName="Giorni"
  docTitle="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Giorni handles your data: what the app collects, why, who processes it, and your rights under the GDPR."
  canonicalUrl="https://rubenspessoa.dev/giorni/privacy/"
  effectiveDate="July 22, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what data the Giorni habit tracker for iPhone collects, why, who
    processes it, and the rights you have. Giorni works without an account, your habit data stays
    on your device and in your own iCloud, and we do not sell or share your data for advertising.
    We operate no server of our own for Giorni.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho
    <br />
    UNESCO-Esplanade 8/55, 8020 Graz, Austria
    <br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a> for full legal details.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

  <h3>Your habits and notes</h3>
  <p>
    The habits you track, your completions, focus sessions, and notes are stored on your device.
    If you use iCloud, they are synced through your own private iCloud storage, which we cannot
    access. This data never reaches servers we operate.
  </p>

  <h3>Reminders</h3>
  <p>
    Habit reminders are local notifications scheduled on your device. They are not sent through a
    server.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    Subscriptions are sold and billed by Apple through the App Store using Apple&rsquo;s StoreKit.
    We never see your payment details, and no third-party purchase service is involved.
  </p>

  <h3>Usage analytics</h3>
  <p>
    We use two analytics services to understand how the app is used &mdash; screens viewed,
    features used, and events such as a completed habit (event names only, not the content of your
    habits or notes):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Amplitude (USA): usage events keyed to an anonymous identifier; we cannot identify you
      personally from it
    </li>
    <li>
      TelemetryDeck (Germany): privacy-focused analytics that anonymizes identifiers before
      storage
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use analytics under our legitimate interest in improving the product.</p>

  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR we process data based on: <strong>performance of a contract</strong> (providing
    the app and your subscription) and <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (product analytics).
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Apple (USA): App Store distribution, payments, device services, iCloud</li>
    <li>Amplitude (USA): product analytics</li>
    <li>TelemetryDeck (Germany): anonymized product analytics</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where providers are located in the USA, transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework
    and/or Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Habit data and notes: only on your device and in your iCloud; deleting the app (and its iCloud data) removes it</li>
    <li>
      Analytics data: per the retention settings of the respective tool, kept only as long as
      needed for the purposes above
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access, rectify, delete, restrict, or receive a copy of your data, and
    to object to processing based on legitimate interest. Because we hold no account for you,
    exercising these rights works by email: write to
    <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>. You also have the
    right to complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (
    <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dsb.gv.at</a>) or
    your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Giorni is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will update it here with a new effective date. Material changes
    will be highlighted in the app.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
